<title>COLOMBIA: Top Colombian reinsurance firm sees profit shrink.</title>
<headline>Top Colombian reinsurance firm sees profit shrink.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's leading reinsurance company, Reaseguradora de Colombia SA, reported a net profit of 29.43 billion pesos in 1996, down sharply from 54.66 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>In its earnings statement, the company gave no official reason for the nosedive in profits and spokesmen could not be reached for immediate comment.</p>
<p>Reaseguradora de Colombia belongs to the powerful Sindicato Antioqueno conglomerate and is one of three reinsurance companies operating across the country.</p>
<p>The company statement said a shareholders' meeting was set for March 17.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
